# __PROJECT_NAME__-main

Project hub for **__PROJECT_NAME__**. A small meta-repo that holds:

- `project.yaml` — registry of all sub-repos
- `AGENTS.md` — project map for AI-assisted work (canonical, agent-neutral)
- `CLAUDE.md` — thin `@AGENTS.md` import (Claude Code compatibility)
- `invoke-ai.sh` — agent picker launcher (claude, omp, …) run across the sub-repos
- `dev-docs/` — product knowledge root: cross-repo architecture, product ADRs, runbooks, processed client deliveries
- `.claude/skills/` — vendored conventions (works without the marketplace plugin)

The actual code lives in subfolders, each its own git repo. The hub's `.gitignore` keeps them out of this repo's history.

## Quick start

```bash
# Clone all registered sub-repos (skips ones you don't have access to)
# Run from a /ws-hub repos clone command inside claude, or manually:
#   git clone <url> ./<name>   for each in project.yaml

# Pick an agent (claude / omp) and launch across all available sub-repos
./invoke-ai.sh
```

## Layout

```
__PROJECT_NAME__-main/
├── project.yaml         # repo registry + conventions version
├── AGENTS.md            # AI project map (canonical, agent-neutral)
├── CLAUDE.md            # thin @AGENTS.md import
├── invoke-ai.sh         # launcher (agent picker)
├── README.md
├── .gitignore           # managed block ignores sub-repo subfolders
├── .claude/skills/      # vendored conventions (works without the plugin)
├── dev-docs/            # product knowledge root (tracked by hub git)
│   ├── architecture.md  # cross-repo synthesis (written by /ws-hub docs)
│   ├── decisions/       # product ADRs
│   ├── runbooks/        # product-level operational runbooks
│   └── scoping/         # processed client deliveries (from /ws-hub intake)
├── openwiki/            # optional derived wiki (only if initialized)
├── __PROJECT_NAME__-app/      # type: working — own git, gitignored
├── __PROJECT_NAME__-design/   # type: input — own git, gitignored
├── __PROJECT_NAME__-client/   # type: input — own git, gitignored
├── __PROJECT_NAME__-docs/     # type: output — own git, gitignored
└── ...                        # add repos via /ws-hub add
```

## Managing the hub

Use the `ws` plugin hub verbs (`/ws-hub <verb>`):

- `init` — initialize a new hub (or adopt existing repos)
- `doctor` — diagnose and repair the hub
- `update` — migrate hub conventions to the latest version (interactive)
- `intake` — process a client delivery into `dev-docs/scoping/`
- `status` — read-only git sweep across all sub-repos
- `repos <pull|clone>` — one git operation across all registered repos
- `add [--scan]` — register a sub-repo (clone / adopt / sibling / mark output)
- `describe` — refresh sub-repo descriptions from their READMEs
- `docs` — generate cross-repo docs via hub-architect (+ wiki refresh offer)
- `explained` — generate the `purpose: explained` product artefacts
